            %strong
              radical
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msqrt
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{I}
              of an ideal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\subset R
            as an ideal
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msqrt
                    %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sqrt{I} = \{ r\in R \,|\, \exists n\in \mathbb{N}, r^n\in I \}
          %p
            An ideal is called a
            %em radical ideal
            if it is equal to its own radical.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilradical"} nilradical
            of a commutative ring is the radical of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            ideal.
          %p
            For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+ring"} noncommutative ring
            or an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            there are many competing notions of a radical of a ring such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobson+radical"} Jacobson radical
          %p
            Given a (possibly noncommutative) ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %em
              radical of an
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is the intersection of all of its maximal submodules. It may also be presented as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+sum"} internal sum
            of all its
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfluous+submodule"} superfluous submodule
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/socle"} socle
          %h2#radical_functors Radical functors
          %p
            Each of the notions of radical mentioned above are functorial, and some of the abstract properties of such functors are used in noncommutative localization theory, when defining so called
            = succeed "." do
              %em radical functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} { }_R Mod
            (left modules over a ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+categories"} Grothendieck categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Shulgeifer60"} Shulgeifer 60
          %p
            We define here radical functors on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} { }_R Mod
          %p
            However they are defined, all notions of radical involve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+functor"} additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfunctors"} subfunctors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo
                        %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: \sigma \hookrightarrow 1_{ _R Mod}
            of the identity on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} { }_R Mod
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} Naturality
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            implies the equation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi σ
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi i
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \circ \sigma i = i \circ i\sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mi i
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma i = i\sigma
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monicity
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %em preradical functors
            (e.g.,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Mirhosseinkhani2010"} Mirhosseinkhani 2010
          %p
            Such a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma: {}_R Mod\to {}_R Mod
            is
            %strong idempotent
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mi i
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi σ
                  %mi σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma i = i\sigma: \sigma\sigma \to \sigma
            is an isomorphism, and is called a
            %strong radical functor
            if in addition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma(M/\sigma(M))=0
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_R Mod
            %em this
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %em preradical functor
          %p
            Following
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Goldman1969"} Goldman 1969
            = succeed "." do
              %strong idempotent kernel functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                  %mo =
                  %mi σ
                  %mi Ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma \sigma M = \sigma Ker(M\to M/\sigma M) = Ker (\sigma M\to \sigma(M/\sigma M)) = Ker(\sigma M\to M\to M/\sigma M) = \sigma M
          %p
            where in the last step, we used that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            is a subfunctor of the identity, hence the compositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma M\hookrightarrow M\to M/\sigma M
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma M\to \sigma(M/\sigma M)\to M/\sigma M
            coincide.
          %p
            However, beware that other authors call a left exact additive subfunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma: {}_R Mod\to {}_R Mod
            of the identity functor a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+functor"} kernel functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            an
            %em idempotent kernel functor
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma(M/\sigma(M))=0
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_R Mod
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "#BuesoJaraVerschoren95"} Bueso-Jara-Verschoren 95
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Example (
            %a{:href => "#BuesoJaraVerschoren95"}> Bueso-Jara-Verschoren 95 2.3.4
            ): Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            be a two-sided ideal in a ring. Define a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : {}_R Mod\to {}_R Mod
            on objects by
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mi M
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi n
                    %mi M
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma M = \{ m\in M\,|\, \exists n, I^n M = 0\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is finitely generated as left
            = succeed "-ideal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-submodule" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is a left exact radical functor. It is clear that the formula for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma M
            reminds the definition of the radical of an ideal of a commutative ring.
          %p
            Nonexample: the subfunctor of identity which to any module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            assigns its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/socle"} socle
            is left exact but not a radical functor.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Shulgeifer60
              %p
                E. G. Shulʹgeĭfer (Е. Г. Шульгейфер),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em К общей теории радикалов в категориях
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathnet.ru/php/getFT.phtml?jrnid=sm&paperid=4826&what=fullt&option_lang=rus"} pdf
            %li#BuesoJaraVerschoren95
              %p
                J. L. Bueso, P. Jara, A. Verschoren,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Compatibility, stability, and sheaves
            %li#Goldman1969
              %p
                O. Goldman,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Rings and modules of quotients
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radical_of_a_ring"} radical of a ring
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radical_of_a_module"} radical of a module
            %li
              %p
                M Grandis, G Janelidze, László Márki,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Non-pointed exactness, radicals, closure operators
                = succeed ":3" do
                  %strong 94
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S1446788713000086"} doi
                %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/431EFE4DD7D116A6ED8EACF22AAD020E/S1446788713000086a.pdf/non-pointed-exactness-radicals-closure-operators.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                D. N. Dikranjan,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical structure of closure operators with applications to topology
